    cat: "geopolitica",
    title: "Watch: What is it like to travel on Air Force One with Trump?",
    summary: "Donald Trump secretly swapped planes as he left a Nato summit in Turkey last month, deceiving even the press pool who flew on board without him.",
    preview: "Watch: What is it like to travel on Air Force One with Trump? President Donald Trump secretly swapped planes as he left a Nato summit in Turkey last month, according to US media. Footage from 8 July shows him boarding Air Force One, the presidential jet, at Ankara airport. But according to the Washington Post, he was then secretly taken to a smaller C-32A military aircraft - a modified Boeing 757 often used by the vice-president - via a catering truck, which had been elevated to plane level on the opposite side to where he had boarded.",
    body: "Watch: What is it like to travel on Air Force One with Trump?\n\nPresident Donald Trump secretly swapped planes as he left a Nato summit in Turkey last month, according to US media. Footage from 8 July shows him boarding Air Force One, the presidential jet, at Ankara airport. But according to the Washington Post, he was then secretly taken to a smaller C-32A military aircraft - a modified Boeing 757 often used by the vice-president - via a catering truck, which had been elevated to plane level on the opposite side to where he had boarded.\n\nJournalists and some White House staff boarded Air Force One and were reportedly told to close their window shades. They were unaware the president was no longer on board.\n\nThe BBC's State Department correspondent Tom Bateman shares what it's like to be onboard Air Force One with the president as part of the press pool.\n\nRelated topics\n\n- United StatesUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- Donald TrumpUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- Iran warUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.",
